      "side": 1,
      "message": "crosvm side here:\n\ncrrev.com/c/4697702\n\nI think the crosvm side and AOSP sides should land roughly at the same time.  The reason is because if we land the crosvm side without AOSP side, other workflows might be worken:\n\nhttps://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu/-/issues/1611",
      "revId": "131a4372e10f52a75d7c5547fabbf242f94295ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56d2f218_47932d10",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-21T20:28:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what the link is about. We need AOSP crosvm and upstream crosvm to be exactly in sync, otherwise some upstream qemu workflow is going to be broken? Sound unsupported to me. Maybe we can chat more to understand what your need is.\n\nUpstream crosvm changes land in AOSP generally within a week. I\u0027d think that would be good enough.\n\nThis is up in the air still, but, in the trunk stable world, we might decide to freeze crosvm imports occasionally for weeks. If we do that, we aren\u0027t going want to make an exception for just rutabaga_gfx changes.",
      "parentUuid": "a3bd193f_a267a9a9",
      "revId": "131a4372e10f52a75d7c5547fabbf242f94295ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e741afc6_b9a2ddac",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101621
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-21T21:26:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We need AOSP crosvm and upstream crosvm to be exactly in sync, otherwise some upstream qemu workflow is going to be broken?\n\nI agree with you there.  the upstream side has already been reviewed, as is ready to merge.  It\u0027s the AOSP merges which typically take more time:\n\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/crosvm/crosvm/+/4697702\n\nBut gfxstream upstream is AOSP, so this needs to land along with that.  \n\nSoonish (\u003c 1 month), the gfxstream API will be stabilized  and an official release (hence QEMU workflow) so it won\u0027t be a recurring problem.\n\nBut gfxstream interface needs to be cleaned up before we could issue an issue release.",
      "parentUuid": "56d2f218_47932d10",
      "revId": "131a4372e10f52a75d7c5547fabbf242f94295ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92038cc5_744e727b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-21T21:50:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still don\u0027t get why you think they need to be in sync. The QEMU folks could just grab a compatible crosvm commit or use the AOSP crosvm repo instead.\n\nAnyways, I don\u0027t have a blocking concern, just wanted to communicate that we might have to push back more in the future. If the API breakages are going settle down soon, them I\u0027m happy :)",
      "parentUuid": "e741afc6_b9a2ddac",
      "revId": "131a4372e10f52a75d7c5547fabbf242f94295ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
